From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:40:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme frame the selected menu row instead of filling it

A menu list's selected row (menus, option lists, quick access, a
game's options) is drawn as a bar of the selector colour, in a
gradient if the theme asks. menutext's selectorPath, selectorCornerSize
and selectorMargin frame that row with a ninepatch instead: the
selection is a border, as on the theme's cards, and neither the bar nor
the hover tint is drawn. Without it nothing changes.
---
 THEMES.md                                |  7 +++++++
 es-core/src/ThemeData.cpp                |  9 +++++++++
 es-core/src/ThemeData.h                  |  5 ++++-
 es-core/src/components/ComponentList.cpp | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++--
 es-core/src/components/ComponentList.h   |  7 +++++++
 5 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/THEMES.md b/THEMES.md
index 17c39d2a..16514ff2 100644
--- a/THEMES.md
+++ b/THEMES.md
@@ -1492,6 +1492,13 @@ BATOCERA 5.24
 	- Lists show whole rows only: they scroll by rows and leave out a row they cannot show whole. Default is false.
 * `valueSpacing` - type: FLOAT. (`menutext` only)
 	- The space between a row's value and its chevron, as a fraction of the screen width. Default is 0.005.
+* `selectorPath` - type: PATH. (`menutext` only)
+	- A ninepatch that frames the selected row (and an option list's, a popup's) instead of the selector bar: the
+	  selection is a border; the bar and its hover tint are not drawn. Default: none (the bar).
+* `selectorCornerSize` - type: FLOAT. (`menutext` only)
+	- That ninepatch's corner size, in pixels.
+* `selectorMargin` - type: FLOAT. (`menutext` only)
+	- The space between the frame and the list's sides, as a fraction of the screen width. Default is 0.
 	
 
 #### menuSwitch
